  "coverage": {
    "mode": "explicit-classified",
    "gaps": [
      "omega-dart states no call argument, so every string a Flutter construct carries is invisible: the path of a GoRoute, the name given to Navigator.pushNamed, the `initialRoute` of a MaterialApp and the routes map. Navigation is therefore recorded as an operation at a site, not as an edge to a named route, and the old route-to-component rule is deleted rather than ported.",
      "omega-yaml publishes a config key's value as an attribute, and an attribute is write-only to the overlay (overlay.rs OverlayFact::field never consults it). So `uses-material-design: true` yields the key and not the truth value, and a font `family: Raleway` cannot be keyed by the family name -- which is why FontFamily and FontFaceSetting are gone.",
      "A bare `MyButton(...)` is a call.function in Dart, indistinguishable from `setState(...)` by anything the Pack states, and the enclosing class cannot be tested for being a widget because a span join relates the call to its class and not the class to its supertype clause. So a project's own widgets are reached through the `const`/`new` spelling and through Flutter's own widget names, not through every construction.",
      "omega-dart publishes no `qualifier`, so no Dart fact carries `external`, and no rule here can name the package a call resolves to. The package is read from the import URI instead.",
      "definition.function spans the signature and not the body, so a call in a method body joins its class but never its method; a per-method attribution is not available."
    ]
